m/users/zasweq/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zasweq/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zasweq/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":0,"closed_issues":60,"state":"closed","created_at":"2022-11-08T21:39:26Z","updated_at":"2023-04-15T01:36:29Z","due_on":"2022-12-27T00:00:00Z","closed_at":"2023-01-10T22:26:16Z"},"comments":0,"created_at":"2022-11-22T02:51:55Z","updated_at":"2023-05-30T01:52:09Z","closed_at":"2022-11-30T19:34:19Z","assignee":{"login":"easwars","id":1638487,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2Mzg0ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1638487?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/easwars","html_url":"https://github.com/easwars","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/easwars/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/easwars/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/easwars/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/easwars/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/easwars/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/easwars/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/easwars/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/easwars/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/easwars/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":"resolved","draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grpc/grpc-go/pulls/5808","html_url":"https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/pull/5808","diff_url":"https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/pull/5808.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/pull/5808.patch","merged_at":"2022-11-30T19:34:19Z"},"body":"This PR is a full-fledged refactor of the transport layer implementation of the xdsclient. It does not touch the existing implementation, and therefore existing implementation will be used until subsequent refactors which will involve the authority/controller/pubsub components.\r\n\r\nSummary of changes:\r\n- New transport implementation in `xds/internal/xdsclient/transport` which supports only xDS v3 transport protocol. We are getting rid of v2 support. So, it does not make sense to add v2 support here. \r\n  - Existing implementation is found in `xds/internal/xdsclient/controller/`.\r\n- New implementation strictly deals only with transport protocol functionality.\r\n  - It exposes an API to send requests for xDS resources. Existing implementation exposes a watch style API. A watch should be a higher layer abstraction and not a transport layer one.\r\n  - The API to send requests needs to contain all the resources to be requested. Transport layer still needs to keep track of the resources being requested because it needs to re-request them upon stream failure.\r\n  - Load reporting API is changed to not accept a server parameter. This is as per federation design. Each transport instance is supposed to talk to *one* management server for both ADS and LRS.\r\n- New Transport API has the following key details\r\n  - Accepts a function to report received resources. This function will be implemented by the data model layer to validate the received resources. The `authority` layer will also keep track of what resources it requested and will cache the received resources.\r\n  - Accepts a function to report stream failures. This is used to propagate stream failures up to the resource watchers at the `authority` layer.\r\n- Tests are in the same directory but in a different package, to ensure that they rely only on functionality and not internal details/state.\r\n\r\nThis refactor ensures that the transport layer has the following properties:\r\n- Has very few dependencies on other parts of the xdsClient.\r\n- Does not look into the resources. That will be the duty of the data model layer.\r\n\r\n#resource-agnostic-xdsclient-api\r\n\r\nRELEASE NOTES: none","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grpc/grpc-go/issues/5808/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grpc/grpc-go/issues/5808/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grpc/grpc-go/issues/3856","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grpc/grpc-go","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grpc/grpc-go/issues/3856/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grpc/grpc-go/issues/3856/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grpc/grpc-go/issues/3856/events","html_url":"https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/pull/3856","id":688322923,"node_id":"MDExOlB1bGxSZXF1ZXN0NDc1NjE0NDg0","number":3856,"title":"xds: v3 support: LRS support","user":{"login":"easwars","id":1638487,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2Mzg0ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1638487?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/easwars","html_url":"https://github.com/easwars","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/easwars/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/easwars/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/easwars/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/easwars/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/easwars/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/easwars/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/easwars/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/easwars/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/easwars/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":586671104,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1ODY2NzExMDQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grpc/grpc-go/labels/Type:%20Feature","name":"T